# Copy this file to `.env.test` (git-ignored, like `.env`) to give `pnpm test` its own database,
# separate from the one `apps/api/.env` points `pnpm dev` at.
#
# Why this exists: the test suites create and delete real rows against whatever DATABASE_URL is active.
# A bug in a test's own cleanup (an unfiltered deleteMany after a failed setup — see src/test-guard.ts)
# once deleted every product, category, product type and template from a shared dev database. Running
# tests against a database that holds nothing you care about makes that class of accident harmless.
#
# `.env.test`, when present, overrides DATABASE_URL for `pnpm test` only (vitest.config.ts) — it never
# touches `pnpm dev`, `pnpm build`, or anything else. CI is unaffected: it sets DATABASE_URL directly on
# the job against its own disposable Postgres container and has no .env.test file to read.
#
# One-time setup on a new machine (same Postgres server as your dev database, a different database
# name on it):
#   1. createdb clothing_brand_test          (or: psql -c "CREATE DATABASE clothing_brand_test;")
#   2. cp .env.test.example .env.test
#   3. pnpm run db:test:migrate              (applies every migration to it)
#   4. pnpm run db:test:seed                 (a handful of tests assume a seeded admin/category exist,
#                                              same as CI's job order: migrate, then seed, then test)
#
# From then on, `pnpm test` (and `pnpm --filter api test`) run against clothing_brand_test automatically.
# Re-run step 3 after pulling a change that adds a migration; the seed in step 4 only needs running once
# (it's idempotent — re-running it is harmless, but tests only ever need it to have run at least once).

DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres@localhost:5432/clothing_brand_test?schema=public
